\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Jesus, the sinner's friend, to Thee,
\par Lost and undone, for aid I flee,
\par Weary of earth, myself, and sin;
\par Open Thine arms, and take me in!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Pity, and heal my sin-sick soul;
\par 'Tis Thou alone canst make me whole;
\par Fall'n, till in me Thine image shine,
\par And cursed I am, till Thou art mine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. At last I own it cannot be
\par That I should fit myself for Thee:
\par Here then to Thee I all resign;
\par Thine is the work, and only Thine.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The mansion for Thyself prepare,
\par Dispose my heart entering there;
\par 'Tis this alone can make me clean,
\par 'Tis this alone can cast out sin.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

